    {
      "dom_id": "question-96563",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-15,-8],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-15$ and $b=-8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(-8-(-15))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{49}{12}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{12}}=\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{6}≈2.021.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
