      "dom_id": "question-130712",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-8,1],$ find $\\text{Var}[X].$",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-8$ and $b=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(1-(-8))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{81}{12}=\\frac{27}{4}.\n$$",
